# SETUP's Advanced page's Spectrogram and the window it opens, ported from
# Controls/SpectrogramUI.cs and ExtLibs/Utilities/Spectrogram.cs (`new SpectrogramUI().Show()`,
# GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigAdvanced.cs:119-122).
#
# The claims: the window opens as its Designer makes it - ACC1 in the combo, Min -80, Max -20,
# three empty graphs X, Y and Z (SpectrogramUI.cs:25-48, SpectrogramUI.Designer.cs:30-188).
# Update before Load Log is the C#'s null `file`, on the status line rather than its box (the
# owner's ruling of 2026-09-25). Load Log reads testdata/dataflash.bin and draws nothing
# (:50-64). ACC2 chosen from the list draws (SelectedIndexChanged) and the fixture has no ACC2,
# so `acc1data[0]` throws - the status line again. The combo is a DropDown, so IMU typed into it
# (no item selected, nothing drawn) and Update draw the fixture's IMU records - three IMUs read as
# one series, 1365 of them: one 1024-sample window's worth, four columns a quarter window apart of
# which two are drawn, AccX, AccY and AccZ in X, Y and Z, coloured from Min to Max
# (Spectrogram.cs:171-247, 322-329). Max's up arrow is ValueChanged, a draw at -19, and more of
# the image is at or above Max. The close box ends it, and the page stays.
#
# No vehicle: the page and the window ask nothing of one; the data directory is a scratch one, so
# no link Mission Planner remembers is opened. Run from the repository root, where the log's path
# is typed relative to, as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-spectrogram.gui
#
# Not yet run: the budget is a guess, set by hand until a passing run records one.

env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK

screen setup
window 1600x1200
budget 13

click setup-page-ConfigAdvanced
expect setup.page ConfigAdvanced
expect config.advanced.buttons.enabled ~ Spectrogram
expect config.spectrogram.window false

# The constructor: the Designer's values, nothing loaded, three empty graphs.
click advanced-BUT_spect
expect config.spectrogram.window true
expect config.spectrogram.opened 1
expect config.spectrogram.sensor ACC1
expect config.spectrogram.sensor.selected 0
expect config.spectrogram.min -80
expect config.spectrogram.max -20
expect config.spectrogram.log none
expect config.spectrogram.running none
expect config.spectrogram.drawn false
expect config.spectrogram.pane.0.title X
expect config.spectrogram.pane.1.title Y
expect config.spectrogram.pane.2.title Z

# Update before Load Log: the C#'s null `file`, on the status line.
click spect-but_redraw
expect config.spectrogram.last Object reference not set to an instance of an object.
expect status Object reference not set to an instance of an object.
expect config.spectrogram.drawn false

# Load Log: its dialog, the fixture typed; read, and nothing drawn.
click spect-but_loadlog
expect config.spectrogram.prompt Load Log
type testdata/dataflash.bin
expect config.spectrogram.prompt.text testdata/dataflash.bin
click spect-open-ok
expect config.spectrogram.prompt none
expect config.spectrogram.log dataflash.bin
expect config.spectrogram.last loaded
expect config.spectrogram.drawn false

# ACC2 from the list: SelectedIndexChanged draws, and the fixture has no ACC2.
click spect-cmb_sensor-arrow
expect config.spectrogram.sensor.list true
click spect-cmb_sensor-1
expect config.spectrogram.sensor.list false
expect config.spectrogram.sensor ACC2
expect config.spectrogram.sensor.selected 1
expect config.spectrogram.last Index was outside the bounds of the array.
expect status Index was outside the bounds of the array.
expect config.spectrogram.drawn false

# IMU typed into the combo: no item selected, nothing drawn; then Update.
click spect-cmb_sensor
key ctrl+u
type IMU
expect config.spectrogram.sensor IMU
expect config.spectrogram.sensor.selected -1
expect config.spectrogram.drawn false
click spect-but_redraw
expect config.spectrogram.last done
expect config.spectrogram.drawn true
expect config.spectrogram.drawn.sensor IMU
expect config.spectrogram.columns 4
expect config.spectrogram.rows 512
expect config.spectrogram.windows 2
expect config.spectrogram.freqmax 1882
expect config.spectrogram.pane.0.field AccX
expect config.spectrogram.pane.1.field AccY
expect config.spectrogram.pane.2.field AccZ
expect config.spectrogram.pane.0.hot 6
expect config.spectrogram.pane.0.cold 24

# Max's up arrow: ValueChanged, a draw at -19.
click spect-num_max-up
expect config.spectrogram.max -19
expect config.spectrogram.last done
expect config.spectrogram.pane.0.hot 4

# The close box; the page stays.
click spect-close
expect config.spectrogram.window false
expect setup.page ConfigAdvanced
expect config.advanced.active true
